      "value": "@{59b9afc4e46c3651b53cf856|full_name}:  Probably. Play area location probably has less to do with it that it's more about how shrunk it is making everything gigantic. The menu is zoomed in & brighter. The text being 5 times the size saying \"use\" or \"equip\" that you can only grab onto one thing (makes sense). I can't even hit the camera icons properly that I don't know where I\"m hitting that I would love actual indicators.\n\nWhen you get very small everything just gets all wacky, zoomed in, and etc that it becomes tricky. When you use the camera you can interact with it somewhat, just not the way you can with 1:1 sized avatars. You can't hit the yellow button, nor the filter, or at all. I can share clips from Twitch of me struggling for 10 minutes to hit any buttons.  \n\nPlay area location probably has less to do with it that it's more about how shrunk it is making everything gigantic. The menu is zoomed in & brighter.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
