      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Let me give comment about large and small avatars.\nI use both in VRChat and put up Stream Camera. So far i can see, it will keep at eye-height, so it's not real problem.\nBut there are avatars with incorrect eye height setup, and that will cause camera will move to another position. It happened me once with avatar from avatar world.\n\nAnd another problem with very small avatars your view camera will cut away your body parts. So extreme small avatars are a problem for VRChat. You will have problem too to grab / press buttons or pick up items in the air, too far for your reach.\n\nAnd for camera interaction, the problem is know the camera box is too dominant and small buttons are hard to reach sometimes. Hopefully this will adjusted soon to make camera use easier.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-10-29T07:32:42.024Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRchat warns that small avatars aren't really supported, and I can see why. I would however love to see \"some\" movement towards supporting small avatars to where using the camera is a breeze. Hard to tell if it's a model issue or VRchat issue, just that I'm noting it here regardless with how people also have small avatars.\n\nI'm using a very tiny avatar (as small as I was told it would get; 15 cm) that I noticed I can't really interact with the camera properly that I would love the blue laser beam to see if I'm even interacting with the camera or not. The radius is weird. This is not just for small avatars either that it would benefit normal sized 1:1 human avatars knowing what you're selecting on the camera; Blue beam you see in the main menu and in some custom worlds. \n\nFor now, I made an alternative model being the standard Hoppu size that should be an adorable middle ground. My new avatar is of Busou Shinki Renge that I also see people favouring & using small avatars for comical effect. Even saw worlds supporting small avatars at times through scenery. What my feature request is more technical with the VR camera & etc with how \"touchy\" and \"blocked out\" it feels. \n\n---------------\n\nSide-note:\n- Desiring a mailing system so people can stay in contact with one another.\n- Bio section in menu so people can contact you if you're a content creator/streamer; Link to discord & etc.\n\n[World is 'Golden Lion' using Shinki Renge avatar desiring small avatars being able to smoothly use cameras with some user feedback of 'blue lasers', or something.]",
